## Iterable — the universal iteration entry point.
##
## Any type that implements `Iterable` gains `.to_iter{}` which returns
## an `Iter 'elem`. All Iter combinators (filter, map, fold, to_seq, …)
## are then available via dot-chaining.
##
## For linear types (List, Deque) the impl is trivial. For non-linear
## types (trees, graphs) the impl delegates to `iter::unfold`. For
## effectful producers (file handles, HTTP streams) effects propagate
## through `<...>` on `to_iter`.
##
## Collections with fused HOFs (Seq, List, Set, SortedSet, Deque) keep
## their direct methods — `Iterable` is for cross-collection pipelines
## and types without built-in fusion.

ability Iterable for 'c having 'elem where {
  to_iter: { it: 'c } -> Iter 'elem <...>
}
